<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.2: Dividing Polynomials Using Long Division</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01614</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.2: Dividing Polynomials Using Long Division</md:title>
    <md:uuid>63cd73f5-b4e5-48b3-8240-6c5b2f206e9b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity </title>
<para>Recall the process of dividing \(960 \div 20\) as a class using long division. Use this same method to divide the polynomials below. After each problem, check in with a partner. With your partner, discuss your work and use the words dividend, divisor, and quotient in your explanations.</para>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the quotient using long division.
        
        \((m^2+9m+20) \div (m+4)\)
      </para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work or look through the video for help. </para>
    <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a9d49c5aee05915f41f403fa42e48dfb7088304d"/></media></problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(m + 5\);</para>
  <para>\[\begin{array}{l}m + 4\mathop{\left){\vphantom{1{{m^2} + 9m + 20}}}\right.
    \!\!\!\!\overline{\,\,\,\vphantom 1{{{m^2} + 9m + 20}}}}
    \limits^{\displaystyle\,\,\, {m\,\, + \,\,5}}\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - ({m^2} + 4m)} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,5m + 20\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline {\, - (5m + 20)} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,0\end{array}\]</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the quotient using long division.
        
        \((p^2+2p-8) \div (p^2-7p+10)\)
      </para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(1+ \frac{9p-18}{p^2-7p+10}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the quotient using long division.
        
        \((5x+5) \div (x+5)\)
      </para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(5- \frac{20}{x+5}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<note>
  <para>Notice in the next problem, there is no \(x^3\) term in the dividend. Add \(0x^3\) as a placeholder when using long division.</para></note>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the quotient using long division.
        
        \((x^4-11x^2-7x-6) \div (x+3)\)
      </para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^3-3x^2-2x-1-\frac{3}{x+3}\)</para>
  <para>\[\begin{array}{l}x + 3\,\,\mathop{\left){\vphantom{1{{x^4} + 0{x^3} -11{x^2} -7x - 6}}}\right.
  \!\!\!\!\overline{\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\vphantom 1{{{x^4} + 0{x^3} -11{x^2} -7x - 6}}}}
  \limits^{\displaystyle {x^3\,\, -3x^2 \,\,-2x\,\,-1}}\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - {x^4} +
  3{x^3}}
  \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-3x^3 -11x^2 -7x
  -6\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline
  {\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, -3{x^3} -9{x^2}}
  \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-2x^2 -7x
  -6\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline {\,
  -2{x^2} -6x}
  \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-x-6\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline
  {\, -x -3}
  \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,-3\end{array}\] </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<note>
  <para>In this next problem, you will need to add two placeholders to divide.</para></note>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the quotient using long division.
        
        \((125x^3-8) \div (5x-2)\)
      </para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para> \(25x^2+10x+4\)</para>
  <para>\[\begin{array}{l}5x - 2\,\,\mathop{\left){\vphantom{1{125{x^3} + 0{x^2} +0x - 8}}}\right.
  \!\!\!\!\overline{\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\vphantom 1{{125{x^3} + 0{x^2} +0x - 8}}}} \limits^{\displaystyle {25^2\,\, +10x
  \,\,+4}}\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - 125{x^3} -50{x^2}}
  \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,50x^2 +0x
  -8\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline {\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, -50{x^2} -20x}
  \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,20x
  -8\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline {\,
  -20x -8}
  \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,0\end{array}\] </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->


<!-- "Start "Are you Ready for More? click to reveal.  If you have more than one on a page, you will need to change the Data-fire/data-wait-for-events for each set.-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem></exercise>
</example><!--Start interaction.  If multiple interactions appear under "are you ready for more?, they should all have matching "data-wait-for-event", which should also match the "data-fire-event" for the button. Note in this sample, they are all RFM1-->
<exercise data-wait-for-event="RFM1">
  <problem>
    <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
    <para>Find the quotient using long division.</para>
    <para>\((125y^5-80y^4-31y^3+37y^2+10y-24) \div (5y-4)\)</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(25y^4+4y^3-3y^2+5y+6\);</para>
    <para>\[\begin{array}{l}5y - 4\mathop{\left){\vphantom{1{125{y^5} - 80{y^4} - 31{y^3} + 37{y^2} + 10y - 24}}}\right.
      \!\!\!\!\overline{\,\,\,\vphantom 1{{125{y^5} - 80{y^4} - 31{y^3} + 37{y^2} + 10y - 24}}}}
      \limits^{\displaystyle\,\,\, {25{y^4} + \,\,\,4{y^3}\,\, - \,\,3{y^2}\,\, + \,\,5y\,\,\, + \,\,6\,}}\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - (125{y^5} - 100{y^4})} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,20{y^4} - 31{y^3}\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - (20{y^4} - 16{y^3})} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, - \,15{y^3} + 37{y^2}\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - ( - \,15{y^3} + 12{y^2})} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,25{y^2} + 10y\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - (25{y^2} - 20y)} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,30y - 24\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - (30y - 24)} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,0\end{array}\]</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--End interaction-->

